        "description": {
            "value": "<p>You rip out a portion of an elemental plane and smash it into your plane, unleashing a chaotic maelstrom. When you Cast this Spell, choose an elemental plane. The collision deals @Damage[8d6[force]] damage and @Damage[8d8[untyped]] damage of a type depending on the chosen plane to each creature in the area with a basic Reflex save. A creature that fails the saving throw is also pushed 25 feet away from the center of the burst (or 50 feet on a critical failure). Each creature whose movement is stopped by a firm surface, such as a well, takes bludgeoning damage equal to the remaining number of feet it would've moved. The area also becomes difficult terrain and hazardous terrain that lasts for a year and a day or until counteracted by a spell or effect such as dispel magic. Any creature that ends its turn in the hazardous terrain takes @Damage[15[untyped]] damage of a type depending on the chosen plane.</p><ul><li><p><strong>Plane of Air</strong> The damage dealt is acid damage, and the spell gains the air trait.</p></li><li><p><strong>Plane of Earth</strong> The damage dealt is bludgeoning damage, and the spell gains the earth trait.</p></li><li><p><strong>Plane of Fire</strong> The damage dealt is fire damage, and the spell gains the fire trait.</p></li><li><p><strong>Plane of Metal</strong> The damage dealt is slashing damage, and the spell gains the metal trait.</p></li><li><p><strong>Plane of Water</strong> The damage dealt is cold damage, and the spell gains the water trait.</p></li><li><p><strong>Plane of Wood</strong> The damage dealt is piercing damage, and the spell gains the wood trait.</p>\n</li></ul>"
        },
